    <string name="ending_usurper_crowned">THE USURPER CROWNED</string>
    <string name="ending_story_true_crown">THE COUNCIL RISES AS ONE AND THE CANDLES ARE SNUFFED IN SALUTE. YOUR PROOF WAS CLEAN ENOUGH THAT NOT A SINGLE MASK DARED SPEAK AGAINST IT.</string>
    <string name="ending_story_quiet_coronation">THE CROWN CHANGES HANDS BEFORE DAWN, WITHOUT TRUMPETS. HALF THE CHAMBER STILL WHISPERS, BUT THE RIGHT HEAD WEARS THE GOLD.</string>
    <string name="ending_story_doubted_heir">YOU NAMED THE RIGHT HEIR ON THIN PROOF. THE COURT OBEYS, YET EVERY CORRIDOR CARRIES A RUMOUR THAT THE JESTER SIMPLY GUESSED WELL.</string>
    <string name="ending_story_silent_council">THE COUNCIL WOULD NOT WAIT FOR YOU. THEY VOTED IN SILENCE, AND THE CHAMBER EMPTIED BEFORE THE LAST SEAL COOLED.</string>
    <string name="ending_story_usurper_crowned">A STRANGER TAKES THE THRONE ON YOUR WORD. THE TRUE HEIR LEAVES BY THE SERVANTS DOOR AND THE JESTER BELLS ARE CUT FROM YOUR CAP.</string>

